<title>HUNGARY: Hungary May PMI index 53.3pct vs 58.0pct in April.</title>
<headline>Hungary May PMI index 53.3pct vs 58.0pct in April.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Purchasing Manager Index (PMI) was 53.3 percent in May, down from 58.0 percent in April, the Hungarian Association of Logistics, Purchasing and Inventory Management (HALPIM) said on Monday. The following is a history of the index over the year on a month-to-month basis:</p>
<p>PURCHASING MANAGER INDEX (Percent)</p>
<p> 1997 April		    58.0</p>
<p>	March		    55.1</p>
<p>	February		 50.4</p>
<p>	January		  46.0</p>
<p> 1996 December		 44.7</p>
<p>	November		 52.8</p>
<p>	October		  57.8</p>
<p>	September		60.4</p>
<p>	August		   52.7</p>
<p>	July		     48.5</p>
<p>	June		     50.6</p>
<p>	May			53.8</p>
<p>	April		    51.4</p>
<p>	March		    51.4</p>
<p>NOTE: The PMI is calculated using the same methodology as the United States' National Association of Purchasing Management Index. A figure above 50 indicates increasing economic activity, while a number below 50 shows declining economic activity.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
